xt{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35148af9-fe39-53be-bd54-85b1a5b3aea3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250129 #edb/ref 1074 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={e}^{x-1},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{1+4i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295388 #edb/ref 1080 "A={\\int }_{-1.5}^{0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295388 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295388 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "15144cc0-d912-5cbb-8bbf-dcd707a34dbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295419 #edb/ref 1080 "A={\\int }_{0}^{-0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295419 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295419 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19d8f3ee-f891-56f8-85a4-4b9d3f48a7ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295524 #edb/ref 1080 "A={\\int }_{1.5}^{3}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295524 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 1